        "original_id": "971fa6ff-d1ab-5585-b7dd-6925b8d8c5e6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Waputik Mountains\n- People: George M. Dawson\n- Animals: Mountain goat, Oreamnos americanus, Rocky Mountain goat\n- Languages and Terms: Stoney Indian word \"waputik\"\n\nFacts:\n- In 1884, George M. Dawson named the Waputik Mountains.\n- The name \"waputik\" is a Stoney Indian word meaning \"white goat.\"\n- The mountain goat is also known as Oreamnos americanus and the Rocky Mountain goat.\n- The mountain goat is a large hoofed mammal endemic to North America.",
